==English==

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/ˈʃəʊd/|a=RP}}
* {{IPA|en|/ˈʃoʊd/|a=GA}}
* {{audio|en|LL-Q1860 (eng)-Persent101-showed.wav|Audio (US)}}

===Verb===
{{head|en|verb form}}

# {{infl of|en|show||spast}}
#: {{ux|en|I '''showed''' him the report.}}
# {{lb|en|US|sometimes|proscribed}} {{past participle of|en|show|nocat=1}} (alternative to [[shown]])
#: {{ux|en|Recent polling has '''showed''' that 40% are in favour of the candidate.}}
#: {{ux|en|The report had already been '''showed''' to him.|q=proscribed}}

====Usage notes====
* ''Garner's Modern American Usage'' favors {{m|en|shown}} over {{m|en|showed}} as past participle and claims it is mandatory for passives. In other forms of English {{m|en|shown}} is the only correct past participle.

